\title{A limit-if-touched order whose trigger watches the last traded price of a different instrument}
\description{
It lets an option be exited when the index crosses a level rather than when the option's own premium spikes in a thin book. A native stop can only watch its own instrument, so this has to run in UBI. UBI does not check that the two instruments are related. \code{trigger_price} here is the level on the watched instrument, not the order's own trigger. With \code{trigger_on}, the level is compared with the bid, the offer or the midpoint instead of the last trade, or must be reached on two ticks in a row (\code{double_last}) or for \code{hold_seconds} (\code{held}), so a single stray trade does not fire it. It answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and sends nothing to a broker until it fires, so keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer. Once it fires, its limit is held in UBI's virtual order book until the other side of the book reaches it, even if the price moves back, unless \code{hold_limits} is \code{FALSE}.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
